          "text": "{\"schema_version\":\"ai-evaluator-v2/1.1\",\"case_id\":\"9-5\",\"candidate_id\":\"candidate_1\",\"action_assessment\":{\"status\":\"preserved\",\"summary\":\"The main business actions are represented with acceptable meaning: receive report, conditionally create account, review for approval, supervisor approve/reject, rejection email, reimbursement, progress email, cancellation email, and resubmission.\"},\"flow_assessment\":{\"status\":\"defect\",\"summary\":\"The graph wrongly forces timeout actions to occur only after approval and makes the 7-day progress-email path terminate instead of allowing later completion, changing required ordering/continuation between timeout actions and eventual completion.\"},\"control_flow_assessment\":{\"status\":\"defect\",\"summary\":\"The 7-day and 30-day deadline behavior is modeled as exclusive post-approval branches. In the source, a 7-day 'approval in progress' email is an intermediate deadline outcome for an unfinished request, not a terminating alternative to reimbursement or later 30-day cancellation.\"},\"main_error_type\":\"wrong_continuation_or_termination\",\"explanation\":\"The source requires deadline handling for unfinished requests: after 7 days the employee receives an 'approval in progress' email, and if still unfinished within 30 days the process stops with cancellation and resubmission. The graph instead places a single timeout decision after approval and treats 'completed in time', 'approval in progress', and 'cancelled' as mutually exclusive outcomes. On the 7-day branch it sends the progress email and then ends the process, so delayed-but-eventually-completed requests cannot proceed to reimbursement, and timeout behavior cannot occur while approval is still pending. Although the core actions and the basic approval/rejection split are present, this materially changes the process behavior.\" ,\"overall_score\":0.56,\"severity\":\"major\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"ambiguity_flag\":false,\"ambiguity_explanation\":\"\",\"requires_human_review\":false,\"review_reason\":\"\"}"
        }
